               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origPlace>
                        <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi</placeName>
                     </origPlace>
                     <origDate notBefore="1850" notAfter="1950">The second half of the 19th century to the first half of the 19th century.</origDate> The manuscript consists of two codicological units. 
                      <ref target="#p1"/> is of smaller size, takes only 3 leaves and was added to the codex later, though most likely around that period.
                  </origin>
                  <provenance>According to <ref target="#coloph1"/>, <persName role="donor" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15283SardaAragawi"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Śarḍa ʾAragāwi</persName> bought the book 
                     and donated it to the <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi</placeName> monastery.  His name connects both codicological units since it appears in the explicit of 
                     <ref target="#p1_i1"/>, and in numerous supplication formulas of <ref target="#p2_i1"/> and  <ref target="#p2_i2"/>.  
                     Additionally, the name <persName role="other" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15284GabraSellase">Gabra Śǝllāse</persName> appears in a few supplication formulas
                     (e.g., <locus target="#52ra #59ra #64vb"/>).</provenance>
               </history>
                     
